# Phase 8a (docs/phase8a-brief.md 3.4, 7.5): the boot escape. RIGHT held at
# power-on opens the Developer list before the shell has reserved anything
# (apps/main.c, HAVE_IPOD_UI_DEVMODE: button_status() & BUTTON_RIGHT).
#   SIM_BUILD=build/sim-ui scripts/shots.sh tests/ui/ipodui-p8a-devmode-boot.script
# needs: library
# boot_keys: RIGHT 2500
# trace: devmode
# log: devmode enter
# log: devmode exit
# golden-region: developer 0 8 320 240
#   (the stock status bar's clock, rows 0-6, reads the host RTC, which
#   sim_clock does not pin: rows 0-7 are skipped, the "Developer" title
#   from its top row 8 on is compared)
#
# The `boot_keys` header holds RIGHT for 2.5 s from the sim's first button
# poll (IPODUI_SIM_BOOT_KEYS, button-sdl.c); an enter with no arm is
# allowed in a boot_keys script. Back from the list continues into the
# shell's main menu. Needs P (main.c boot escape) and U2 (devmode.c);
# PENDING until both land. If the main.c check runs later than 2.5 s
# after the first poll in the sim, raise the hold here (and say so).
# env: SIM_TRACE_LCD_PUSH=1

wait 2000
shot developer      # the stock list before the shell starts
wheel -1            # the Back row, the last (MENU is not cancel in the stock lists)
wait 400
key SELECT          # Back
wait 3000
shot main           # the shell's main menu
quit
